# Local development (`npm run dev`) works with no secrets at all. To try the optional ones, copy this file
# to .dev.vars (git-ignored) and uncomment what you want. For a deployed Worker, set them with
# `wrangler secret put <NAME>` or in the Cloudflare dashboard instead.

# Optional. Without it, the first admin can be created by whoever opens the app first. With it, setup needs this key.
# SETUP_KEY=choose-a-one-time-password

# Optional. Without it, SDS EZY generates a random signing key and keeps it in the database.
# SESSION_SECRET=a-long-random-string

# Optional. Setting this turns on emailed two-factor login codes (see README).
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional. Your own AI key (otherwise Cloudflare Workers AI is used, or an admin can paste a key into Settings).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxx
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxx
# GEMINI_API_KEY=xxxxxxxx

# Optional. Turns the app into a read-only demo (see the README). Use a SEPARATE database for a demo.
# DEMO_MODE=1
# DEMO_ADMIN_EMAIL=demo-admin@example.invalid
# DEMO_USER_EMAIL=demo-user@example.invalid
